\f1\b0  \'97 your physical laptop/desktop running VirtualBox or VMware Workstation Player. This is the only machine with any bridge to the real world, and only for downloading ISOs.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Management LAN (10.10.10.0/24)
\f1\b0  \'97 where your Kali attacker box lives. This is the "trusted" segment in Month 3.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 DMZ segment (10.10.20.0/24)
\f1\b0  \'97 where the Metasploitable victim box lives once pfSense is introduced in Month 3. Before that, in Months 1\'962, both VMs simply sit together on one flat internal network while you learn.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 pfSense firewall VM
\f1\b0  \'97 introduced in Month 3, has three virtual NICs: one facing the isolated lab (acts as WAN for the exercise), one to the management LAN, one to the DMZ. It becomes the chokepoint all traffic must pass through.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

